ex:H19R02 a ct:Rule ;
    rdfs:label "Main agreement requires written material-breach notice and thirty-day cure" ;
    ct:description """TERMINATION

Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in Attachments A, G or H, neither party can suspend its further performance, terminate this Agreement or require specific performance of the other party of this Agreement in whole or in part as a result of the other party's material breach of the terms and conditions of this Agreement without first providing notice to such party in writing and thirty (30) days' opportunity to cure the material breach (and then only if such party fails to cure such breach).""" ;
    ct:kind "TERMINATION" ;
    ct:qualifies ex:H19R01 ;
    ct:subject_to ex:H19R02C ;
    ct:supported_by ex:H19R02P .

ex:H19R02C a ct:Condition ;
    rdfs:label "Expressly applies notwithstanding Attachments A, G or H; do not use conflicting attachment wording without this qualification." ;
    ct:description "Expressly applies notwithstanding Attachments A, G or H; do not use conflicting attachment wording without this qualification." ;
    ct:supported_by ex:H19R02P .

ex:H19R03 a ct:Rule ;
    rdfs:label "Main-agreement change-in-circumstances termination limited by law-compliance requirement" ;
    ct:description """CHANGE IN CIRCUMSTANCES

Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in Attachments A, G or H, in connection with any Change in Circumstances (as defined below), and without limiting Seller's/ExxonMobil Selling Affiliate's other rights under this Agreement or applicable law, Seller/ExxonMobil Selling Affiliates shall have the right: (i) only if required to enable Seller/ExxonMobil Selling Affiliate to comply with applicable laws and regulations, to terminate this Agreement and accelerate all amounts due from Buyer hereunder, making them immediately payable (ii) to modify the payment terms hereunder; and/or (iii) to require that Buyer/Buyer Affiliates pay in advance for shipments hereunder.""" ;
    ct:kind "TERMINATION" ;
    ct:qualifies ex:H19R01 ;
    ct:references_section ex:H19R03F0 ;
    ct:subject_to ex:H19R03C ;
    ct:supported_by ex:H19R03P .

ex:H19R03C a ct:Condition ;
    rdfs:label "Expressly notwithstanding Attachments A/G/H; other notice and defined-event requirements remain." ;
    ct:description "Expressly notwithstanding Attachments A/G/H; other notice and defined-event requirements remain." ;
    ct:supported_by ex:H19R03P .

ex:H19R03F0 a ct:Reference ;
    rdfs:label "Change in Circumstances definition and notice requirements" ;
    ct:resolution_status "UNRESOLVED" .

ex:H20R01C a ct:Condition ;
    rdfs:label "Additional two-year period requires written consent of both parties; accrued obligations survive." ;
    ct:description "Additional two-year period requires written consent of both parties; accrued obligations survive." ;
    ct:supported_by ex:H20R01P .

ex:H20R02 a ct:Rule ;
    rdfs:label "Material breach, company-specific grounds and mutual consent" ;
    ct:description """6.02.  Termination. This Agreement may be terminated only:

(a)  By either party for substantial breach of any material provision of this Agreement by the other, provided due notice has been given to the other of the alleged breach and such other party has not cured the breach within (30) days] thereof; or

(b)  By the Company if: there is an unacceptable change in the control or management of the Distributor; if the Distributor  makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors; if a petition in bankruptcy is filed by or against the Distributor, resulting in an adjudication of bankruptcy; or, if the Distributor fails to pay its debts as they become due and provided due notice has been given by the Company to the Distributor and the Distributor has not cured such breach within thirty (30) days thereof; or   (c)  By the written consent of both parties;

                (d)  Upon termination of this Agreement all further rights and obligations of the parties shall cease, except that Distributor shall not be relieved of (i) its obligation to pay any monies due, or to become due, as of or after the date of termination, and (ii) any other obligation set forth in this Agreement which is to take effect after the date of termination.""" ;
    ct:kind "TERMINATION" ;
    ct:qualifies ex:H20R01 ;
    ct:subject_to ex:H20R02C ;
    ct:supported_by ex:H20R02P .

ex:H20R02C a ct:Condition ;
    rdfs:label "Preserve thirty-day cure and listed change-of-control, bankruptcy and other grounds; surviving obligations remain." ;
    ct:description "Preserve thirty-day cure and listed change-of-control, bankruptcy and other grounds; surviving obligations remain." ;
    ct:supported_by ex:H20R02P .

ex:H01R01P a ct:SourcePassage ;
    ct:end_char 7840 ;
    ct:exact_text "7.1  Unless  otherwise  stated  in  the  Appendix  the  term of this letter           Agreement  shall  continue  for  twenty-four  (24)  months  with  the           effective  date  unless  terminated sooner or extended pursuant to the           terms hereof (\"Initial Term\"). The Initial Term shall automatically be           extended  for  an additional period of half a year unless either party           provides  the  other party with written notification of termination of           the  letter  Agreement  at  least 60 days prior to end of such period." ;
    ct:source_path "cuad/DataCallTechnologies_20060918_SB-2A_EX-10.9_944510_EX-10.9_Content License Agreement.txt" ;
    ct:source_sha256 "20f0f1630d8ae7ba221fbbf9d0449a593605989dfa3c779cafdb9c233bb6ebe7" ;
    ct:start_char 7280 .

ex:H01R02P a ct:SourcePassage ;
    ct:end_char 8540 ;
    ct:exact_text """7.2  Either  Party  shall  be  entitled  to  cancel  this  Agreement if the           other Party is materially in breach of the terms of this Agreement. If           the  breach  of  contract is capable of being remedied, this Agreement           can  be  cancelled  only  provided  that  the  Party in breach has not           rectified  its breach within thirty (30) days of the written notice by           the  other  Party.

     7.3  Either  Party  may  cancel  this  Agreement  already prior to the date           of  its  fulfillment,  if it becomes evident that the other Party will           commit  a  breach  of  contract  entitling  to  cancellation  of  this           Agreement.""" ;
    ct:source_path "cuad/DataCallTechnologies_20060918_SB-2A_EX-10.9_944510_EX-10.9_Content License Agreement.txt" ;
    ct:source_sha256 "20f0f1630d8ae7ba221fbbf9d0449a593605989dfa3c779cafdb9c233bb6ebe7" ;
    ct:start_char 7847 .

ex:H01R04P a ct:SourcePassage ;
    ct:end_char 13841 ;
    ct:exact_text """2.1  Contract  start:  04-01-06

     2.2  Contract  end:  04-01-08

     2.3  Commercial  distribution  possible  from:

     2.4  Sell-off  period:  3  months  after  termination""" ;
